r(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">rig_task_id</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">string</dd><dd class="rounded-md bg-red-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-red-600 dark:bg-red-500/10 dark:text-red-400">Required</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>The ID of the Rigging task whose character to animate, from <code>POST /openapi/v1/rigging</code>. The task must have the status <code>SUCCEEDED</code>.</p></dd></dl></li></ul></div><div class="border-b border-zinc-900/20 dark:border-white/10"></div><p>Send exactly one of <code>action_id</code>, <code>action_ids</code>, and <code>motion_task_id</code>.</p><div class="my-6"><ul role="list" class="list-none divide-y divide-zinc-900/20 p-0 dark:divide-white/10 ml-0"><li class="m-0 px-0 py-4 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2"><dt class="sr-only">Name</dt><dd><span class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-code-ring)] dark:bg-[color:var(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">action_id</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">integer</dd><dd class="rounded-md bg-red-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-red-600 dark:bg-red-500/10 dark:text-red-400">Required</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>Required unless you send <code>action_ids</code> or <code>motion_task_id</code>. The ID of the preset animation to apply. For the full list of animations, see the <a class="text-meshy-700 hover:text-meshy-800 dark:text-meshy-500 dark:hover:text-meshy-300 inline-flex justify-center items-center" href="/api/animation-library" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Animation Library reference<svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="h-4 w-4"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M6.04159 5.83331C6.04159 5.48814 6.32141 5.20831 6.66659 5.20831H14.1666C14.5118 5.20831 14.7916 5.48814 14.7916 5.83331V13.3333C14.7916 13.6785 14.5118 13.9583 14.1666 13.9583C13.8214 13.9583 13.5416 13.6785 13.5416 13.3333V7.3422L6.27519 14.6086C6.03112 14.8527 5.63539 14.8527 5.39131 14.6086C5.14723 14.3645 5.14723 13.9688 5.39131 13.7247L12.6577 6.45831H6.66659C6.32141 6.45831 6.04159 6.17849 6.04159 5.83331Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a> or <a href="#list-animations">List animations</a>.</p></dd></dl></li></ul></div><div class="my-6"><ul role="list" class="list-none divide-y divide-zinc-900/20 p-0 dark:divide-white/10 ml-0"><li class="m-0 px-0 py-4 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2"><dt class="sr-only">Name</dt><dd><span class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-code-ring)] dark:bg-[color:var(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">action_ids</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">array of integers</dd><dd class="rounded-md bg-red-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-red-600 dark:bg-red-500/10 dark:text-red-400">Required</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>Required unless you send <code>action_id</code> or <code>motion_task_id</code>. The IDs of 1 to 10 preset animations to apply at once, with no repeats. More than 10 IDs, or a repeated ID, returns <code>400</code>. For the IDs, see the <a class="text-meshy-700 hover:text-meshy-800 dark:text-meshy-500 dark:hover:text-meshy-300 inline-flex justify-center items-center" href="/api/animation-library" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Animation Library reference<svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="h-4 w-4"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M6.04159 5.83331C6.04159 5.48814 6.32141 5.20831 6.66659 5.20831H14.1666C14.5118 5.20831 14.7916 5.48814 14.7916 5.83331V13.3333C14.7916 13.6785 14.5118 13.9583 14.1666 13.9583C13.8214 13.9583 13.5416 13.6785 13.5416 13.3333V7.3422L6.27519 14.6086C6.03112 14.8527 5.63539 14.8527 5.39131 14.6086C5.14723 14.3645 5.14723 13.9688 5.39131 13.7247L12.6577 6.45831H6.66659C6.32141 6.45831 6.04159 6.17849 6.04159 5.83331Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a>.</p><p>Meshy returns one file with one animation clip per action, which suits a state machine in a game engine. Meshy charges for each action in the list. See <a href="/en/api/pricing">Pricing</a>.</p><p>A list with one ID works the same as sending that ID as <code>action_id</code>.</p></dd></dl></li></ul></div><div class="my-6"><ul role="list" class="list-none divide-y divide-zinc-900/20 p-0 dark:divide-white/10 ml-0"><li class="m-0 px-0 py-4 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2"><dt class="sr-only">Name</dt><dd><span class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-code-ring)] dark:bg-[color:var(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">motion_task_id</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">string</dd><dd class="rounded-md bg-red-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-red-600 dark:bg-red-500/10 dark:text-red-400">Required</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>Required unless you send <code>action_id</code> or <code>action_ids</code>. The ID of a <a class="text-meshy-700 hover:text-meshy-800 dark:text-meshy-500 dark:hover:text-meshy-300 inline-flex justify-center items-center" href="/api/text-to-motion" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Text to Motion<svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="h-4 w-4"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M6.04159 5.83331C6.04159 5.48814 6.32141 5.20831 6.66659 5.20831H14.1666C14.5118 5.20831 14.7916 5.48814 14.7916 5.83331V13.3333C14.7916 13.6785 14.5118 13.9583 14.1666 13.9583C13.8214 13.9583 13.5416 13.6785 13.5416 13.3333V7.3422L6.27519 14.6086C6.03112 14.8527 5.63539 14.8527 5.39131 14.6086C5.14723 14.3645 5.14723 13.9688 5.39131 13.7247L12.6577 6.45831H6.66659C6.32141 6.45831 6.04159 6.17849 6.04159 5.83331Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a> task whose clip to apply instead of a preset action. The task must have the status <code>SUCCEEDED</code>, and the rig must be a biped.</p><p>Meshy retargets the clip onto the rigged character. It copies the clip when you create this task, so this task isn&#x27;t affected if the Text to Motion task later expires or you delete it. Meshy keeps the Text to Motion task&#x27;s files for 3 days, so apply the clip before then.</p></dd></dl></li></ul></div><div class="border-b border-zinc-900/20 dark:border-white/10"></div><div class="my-6"><ul role="list" class="list-none divide-y divide-zinc-900/20 p-0 dark:divide-white/10 ml-0"><li class="m-0 px-0 py-4 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2"><dt class="sr-only">Name</dt><dd><span class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-code-ring)] dark:bg-[color:var(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">post_process</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">object</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>Post-processing for the animation output. Leave it out to get the standard animation files.</p><p>With <code>motion_task_id</code>, the retarget can produce a GLB-only animation. If you send <code>post_process</code> and no FBX file is available, the task fails with a <code>task_error</code>, and Meshy refunds your credits. Without <code>post_process</code>, the task succeeds, and <code>animation_fbx_url</code> is empty.</p></dd></dl></li></ul></div><div class="my-6 ml-4"><div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-700"><div class="border-b border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 px-5 py-2.5 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-800/50"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Applies only when<!-- --> <code class="rounded bg-zinc-200/70 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">post_process</code> is set</span></div><div class="px-5"><ul role="list" class="list-none divide-y divide-zinc-900/20 p-0 dark:divide-white/10"><li class="m-0 px-0 py-4 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2"><dt class="sr-only">Name</dt><dd><span class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-code-ring)] dark:bg-[color:var(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">operation_type</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">string</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>The operation to run. Without it, Meshy makes no extra file. A value not in the following list returns <code>400</code>.</p><p>Available values:</p><ul>
<li><code>change_fps</code>: changes the frame rate to <code>fps</code></li>
