0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">search</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">string</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>Text to search for. Meshy returns the animations whose <code>name</code> or <code>key</code> contains this text, ignoring case. Meshy matches the text literally, so <code>%</code> and <code>_</code> aren&#x27;t wildcards.</p></dd></dl></li><li class="m-0 px-0 py-4 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2"><dt class="sr-only">Name</dt><dd><span class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-code-ring)] dark:bg-[color:var(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">category</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">string</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>The category to list, as an exact match. An unknown category returns an empty list.</p><p>Available values:</p><ul>
<li><code>WalkAndRun</code></li>
<li><code>BodyMovements</code></li>
<li><code>DailyActions</code></li>
<li><code>Fighting</code></li>
<li><code>Dancing</code></li>
</ul></dd></dl></li><li class="m-0 px-0 py-4 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2"><dt class="sr-only">Name</dt><dd><span class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-code-ring)] dark:bg-[color:var(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">sub_category</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">string</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>The subcategory to list, as an exact match. You can send it without <code>category</code>. Subcategory names aren&#x27;t unique across categories. For example, <code>Transitioning</code> is under both <code>Fighting</code> and <code>DailyActions</code>. So without <code>category</code>, the filter matches the subcategory in every category.</p></dd></dl></li><li class="m-0 px-0 py-4 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><dl class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2"><dt class="sr-only">Name</dt><dd><span class="rounded-lg bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-code-ring)] dark:bg-[color:var(--tw-prose-invert-code-bg)] dark:text-zinc-100 dark:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--tw-prose-invert-code-ring)]">action_ids</span></dd><dt class="sr-only">Type</dt><dd class="rounded-md bg-teal-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:bg-teal-500/10 dark:text-teal-400">string</dd><dt class="sr-only">Description</dt><dd class="w-full flex-none [&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p>The animations to return, as up to 200 comma-separated <code>action_id</code> values. Use it to look up specific IDs instead of browsing. More than 200 IDs returns <code>400</code>.</p><p>The response leaves out an ID that no animation has. So you can also use this filter to check whether IDs you stored are still available.</p></dd></dl></li></ul></div><h3 class="scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-h)+2rem)] text-base pb-2 mb-4">Combining filters</h3><p>Meshy applies the filters together. Each one narrows the result, so Meshy returns an animation only if it matches all of them. Within one filter, any of its values can match. For example, <code>search</code> matches <code>name</code> or <code>key</code>, and <code>action_ids</code> matches any ID in the list.</p><p>So a combination with no overlap returns an empty array, not an error. Action <code>92</code> is &quot;Double Combo Attack&quot;, a <code>Fighting</code> animation. For example:</p><ul>
<li><code>?action_ids=92&amp;category=Fighting</code> returns action <code>92</code>.</li>
<li><code>?action_ids=92&amp;category=Dancing</code> returns <code>[]</code>, because it isn&#x27;t a <code>Dancing</code> animation.</li>
<li><code>?action_ids=92&amp;search=walk</code> returns <code>[]</code>, because its name doesn&#x27;t match <code>walk</code>.</li>
</ul><p>To get specific animations in any category, send <code>action_ids</code> on its own.</p><h3 class="scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-h)+2rem)] text-base pb-2 mb-4">Returns</h3><p>A list of <a href="#the-animation-object">animation objects</a>.</p><div data-note="true" class="my-6 flex gap-2.5 rounded-2xl border border-meshy-500/70 bg-meshy-100/50 p-4 leading-6 text-zinc-800 dark:border-meshy-500/30 dark:bg-meshy-500/5 dark:text-meshy-200 dark:[--tw-prose-links-hover:theme(colors.meshy.300)] dark:[--tw-prose-links:theme(colors.white)]"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 h-4 w-4 flex-none fill-meshy-800 stroke-white dark:fill-meshy-200/20 dark:stroke-meshy-200"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="8" stroke-width="0"></circle><path fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M6.75 7.75h1.5v3.5"></path><circle cx="8" cy="4" r=".5" fill="none"></circle></svg><div class="[&amp;&gt;:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;:last-child]:mb-0"><p><a href="#create-an-animation-task">Create an Animation task</a> accepts every <code>action_id</code> this endpoint returns, and this endpoint returns every ID that create accepts. Neither includes retired animations. If you cache the library, refresh it from time to time, so a retired ID doesn&#x27;t stay in your picker.</p></div></div></div></div>
